  "name": "Ducker",
  "description": "Use a kick to duck a stereo bass. Route bass → Ducker Audio and Ducker Stereo Output → Master. Remove the parallel bass-to-Master route. Send the kick to Ducker Control and keep its own route to Master. The louder Control channel’s RMS drives both Audio channels. At 0.25 RMS the reduction is half the Depth setting in dB. At 0.5 RMS and above it reaches full Depth. Attack and Release set the envelope half-times. Start with 5 ms Attack, 150 ms Release and 12 dB Depth. All three controls update during playback.",
